From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:14:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: take the first binder node that exists

The MAINLINE branch of setupBinderNodes() walks BINDER_DRIVERS,
VNDBINDER_DRIVERS and HWBINDER_DRIVERS without stopping at a match, so
the last node found wins. The lists put Waydroid's own anbox-* nodes
first, so wherever both exist the container gets the plain /dev/binder.

On a Halium host that node belongs to the host's Android. A vendor that
sets no ro.vndk.version - the BraX3's SDK 36 vendor has none - makes
get_vendor_type() answer MAINLINE, so the container shared the host
binder. Its vold then could not register with a service manager that
already has a vold ("Unable to start VoldNativeService"), and init
rebooted the container two seconds into every start
("reboot,vold-failed").

Stop at the first match, as the HALIUM branch is meant to. Hosts with
only the plain nodes get the same result as before.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/helpers/drivers.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/helpers/drivers.py b/tools/helpers/drivers.py
index 3045ee5..b7279df 100644
--- a/tools/helpers/drivers.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/drivers.py
@@ -124,10 +124,18 @@ def setupBinderNodes(args):
     has_hwbinder = False
     if args.vendor_type == "MAINLINE":
         probeBinderDriver(args)
+        # Take the first node that exists. The lists put Waydroid's own
+        # anbox-* nodes ahead of the plain ones, and without the break the
+        # last match won instead - the host's /dev/binder wherever both exist.
+        # On a Halium host whose vendor sets no ro.vndk.version (the BraX3's
+        # SDK 36 vendor has none) the vendor type comes out MAINLINE, and sharing
+        # the host Android's binder makes the container's vold fail to register
+        # with a service manager that already has one, so init reboots it.
         for node in BINDER_DRIVERS:
             if os.path.exists("/dev/" + node):
                 has_binder = True
                 args.BINDER_DRIVER = node
+                break
         if not has_binder:
             raise OSError('Binder node "binder" for waydroid not found')
 
@@ -135,6 +143,7 @@ def setupBinderNodes(args):
             if os.path.exists("/dev/" + node):
                 has_vndbinder = True
                 args.VNDBINDER_DRIVER = node
+                break
         if not has_vndbinder:
             raise OSError('Binder node "vndbinder" for waydroid not found')
 
@@ -142,6 +151,7 @@ def setupBinderNodes(args):
             if os.path.exists("/dev/" + node):
                 has_hwbinder = True
                 args.HWBINDER_DRIVER = node
+                break
         if not has_hwbinder:
             raise OSError('Binder node "hwbinder" for waydroid not found')
     else:
